message.content:
Dog shampoos are generally classified in heading 3305 (preparations for use on the hair), subheading 3305.10, shampoos. CBP rulings on pet shampoos have gone both ways. Some place them in 3307.90 (other perfumery, cosmetic or toilet preparations), and others in 3305.10. Where the shampoo is a cleansing product for the coat, rulings often cite 3305.10.00 as "Shampoos". Some rulings, however, held that pet shampoos are not "hair" preparations and used 3307.90.00 instead. Items with insecticidal claims would go to 3808, but nothing here suggests that.

I recall NY rulings classifying dog shampoos and conditioners in 3307.90.0000, since heading 3305 covers preparations for human hair. The 3307 heading covers "other" toilet preparations, and the HTSUS 3307.90.00 line is "Other" with statistical suffixes 3307.90.3000 for depilatories and 3307.90.6000 for other. Rulings for pet shampoos, such as those for Burt's Bees dog shampoo, used 3307.90.0000, so I will go with 3307.90.0000. The tariff has since been reorganized: 3307.90.00 has 10-digit statistical numbers, with 3307.90.0000 as the general line. I will answer with that.

{"hts_code": "3307.90.0000", "reason": "Retail-packaged dog shampoos are other toilet/grooming preparations not for human hair, so they fall under heading 3307 as 'other' rather than heading 3305 hair shampoos."}
